===Other personnel===
[[Jamie Fly]], former Radio Free Europe president and CEO, serves as senior counselor to the CEO.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Daniels |first1=Eugene |last2=Lizza |first2=Ryan |last3=Bade |first3=Rachael |date=September 6, 2023 |title=Playbook: An Obama vet's message on Biden bedwetting |url=https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2023/09/06/an-obama-vets-message-on-biden-bedwetting-00114179 |access-date=November 19, 2023 |website=Politico |language=en |archive-date=November 19, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231119002628/https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2023/09/06/an-obama-vets-message-on-biden-bedwetting-00114179 |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Fabrice Brégier]] is president of Palantir France. He is the former COO and president of commercial aircraft at [[Airbus]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Interview with Fabrice Brégier, President of Palantir France |url=https://www.palantir.com/interview-with-fabrice-bregier-president-of-palantir-france/ |publisher=Palantir |access-date=October 22, 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=United States/France • Palantir nabs Fabrice Bregier - 26/09/2018 |url=https://www.intelligenceonline.com/corporate-intelligence/2018/09/26/palantir-nabs-fabrice-bregier,108325301-art |work=Intelligence Online |date=September 26, 2018 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Airbus Board of Directors Announces Top Management Succession Plan |url=https://www.airbus.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2017-12-airbus-board-of-directors-announces-top-management-succession-plan |publisher=Airbus |access-date=October 22, 2025 |language=en |date=October 28, 2021}}</ref> Koichi Narasaki is CEO of Palantir Japan. Previously, he was group chief digital officer of [[SOMPO Holdings]], with which Palantir has a joint venture.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Ben-Hutta |first1=Avi |title=Sompo and Palantir cofound Palantir Japan |url=https://coverager.com/sompo-and-palantir-cofound-palantir-japan/ |work=Coverager - Insurance news and insights |date=November 19, 2019 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Cordon |first1=Miguel |title=Tech in Asia - Connecting Asia's startup ecosystem |url=https://www.techinasia.com/palantir-launches-joint-venture-sompo |work=techinasia.com |date=November 20, 2019}}</ref> Louis Mosley is the head and executive vice president of Palantir Technologies UK.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Church |first1=Sophie |title=Palantir Boss Louis Mosley: Keir Starmer 'Gets' AI, 'You Could See In His Eyes' |url=https://www.politicshome.com/news/article/palantir-boss-interview-keir-starmer-gets-ai |work=Politics Home |date=April 4, 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Science, Innovation and Technology Committee Oral evidence: Digital centre of government, HC 790 |url=https://committees.parliament.uk/oralevidence/16290/html/ |website=committees.parliament.uk |access-date=October 25, 2025}}</ref> Details about Palantir Korea's boards of directors are not fully known, but one board member is Shawn Pelsinger, who is also [[Acrisure]]'s chief administrative officer.<ref>{{cite web |title=8-K |url=https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1936224/000119312525234632/srfm-20251007.htm |publisher=Securities and Exchange Commission |access-date=October 22, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Jimenez-Sanchez |first1=Kassandra |title=Acrisure appoints Pelsinger Chief Administrative Officer, Wassersug named CTO – Reinsurance News |url=https://www.reinsurancene.ws/acrisure-appoints-pelsinger-chief-administrative-officer-wassersug-named-cto/ |work=ReinsuranceNe.ws |date=April 9, 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

As a firm doing sensitive work for governments, Palantir has connections with politicians, and some of its former employees have become public officials. This type of relationship (sometimes called a "revolving door") can cause controversy.<ref name="ft1" /><ref name="techtransparency">{{cite web |title=TTP – Inside Palantir's Expanding Influence Operation |url=https://www.techtransparencyproject.org/articles/inside-palantirs-expanding-influence-operation |publisher=Tech Transparency Project |access-date=October 22, 2025 |language=en-us}}</ref> {{interlanguage link|Laura Rudas|de}} is the executive vice president of strategy.<ref name="MSC2025">{{cite web |title=Munich Security Conference 2025 List of Confirmed Participants (alphabetical) |url=https://securityconference.org/assets/01_Bilder_Inhalte/02_Formate/01_Muenchner-Sicherheitskonferenz/2025/MSC_2025_List_of_Participants_WS.pdf |publisher=Munich Security Conference |access-date=October 22, 2025}}</ref> She is a former Austrian politician, having served as secretary-general of the [[Social Democratic Party of Austria|Social Democrats]] and as a member of the [[National Council (Austria)|Austrian Parliament]]. She left for Palantir despite having won a national reelection campaign.<ref>{{cite news |title=Laura Rudas bei Palantir: Im Dunstkreis der Geheimdienste |url=https://www.derstandard.at/story/2000022042857/laura-rudas-bei-palantir-im-dunstkreis-der-geheimdienste |work=Der Standard |date=September 11, 2015 |language=de-AT}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Laura Rudas |url=https://milkeninstitute.org/events/global-conference-2019/speakers/laura-rudas |publisher=Milken Institute |access-date=October 22, 2025 |language=en}}</ref> [[Mike Gallagher (American politician)|Mike Gallagher]], former [[United States House Select Committee on Strategic Competition between the United States and the Chinese Communist Party|Chair of the House Committee on the Chinese Communist Party]] (2023–2024), is head of defense.<ref name="MSC2025" />

French politician Julie Martinez ([[Socialist Party (France)|Socialist Party]]) is the global data protection officer (she has worked for Palantir for three years) and her party's spokesperson, having been appointed to this office in September 2025. She and Palantir's reputation have caused controversy in France, but her party says the situation is not problematic. She also heads the think tank France Positive.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Champaigne-Kitetoa |first1=Antoine |title=Porte-Parole du Parti socialiste et " en même temps " Global Data Protection Officer chez Palantir |website=Reflets.info |url=https://reflets.info/articles/porte-parole-du-parti-socialiste-et-en-meme-temps-gobal-data-protection-officer-chez-palantir |date=September 6, 2025 |language=fr-FR}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Gastineau |first1=Nicolas |title=Julie Martinez, une " hobbit " socialiste made in Palantir |url=https://revue21.fr/article/julie-martinez-ps-palantir/ |work=Revue21.fr |date=September 19, 2025 |language=fr}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Fleury |first1=Elisabeth |title=IA : la porte-parole du PS travaille chez Palantir, l'ogre de la surveillance algorithmique choyé par Donald Trump – L'Humanité |url=https://www.humanite.fr/politique/big-data/la-porte-parole-du-ps-pour-lia-travaille-chez-palantir-le-geant-de-la-surveillance-algorithmique-choye-par-donald-trump |work=humanite.fr |date=September 5, 2025 |language=fr-FR}}</ref>

[[David MacNaughton]], former [[List of ambassadors of Canada to the United States|ambassador of Canada to the United States]] (2016–2019), is president of Palantir Technologies Canada. He resigned his ambassadorship to join the firm. His activities involving Palantir before and after his resignation have been controversial.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Blatchford |first1=Andy |title=Former Canadian envoy to Washington defends work pitching for Palantir |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2020/05/07/canada-ambassador-palantir-243721 |access-date=October 22, 2025 |work=Politico |date=May 7, 2020 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Yakabuski |first1=Konrad |title=Opinion: The murky business of Canada's former U.S. ambassador |url=https://www.theglobeandmail.com/opinion/article-the-murky-business-of-canadas-former-us-ambassador/ |work=The Globe and Mail |date=June 17, 2020 |language=en-CA}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Tunney |first1=Catharine |title=Freeland, Vance and several federal officials barred from official dealings with ex-ambassador |url=https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/palantir-macnaughton-ethics-1.5726443 |date=September 16, 2020}}</ref> [[Jacob Helberg]], former senior advisor to Karp, is now the U.S. [[Under Secretary of State for Economic Growth, Energy, and the Environment]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Lavers |first1=Michael K. |title=Vance swears in gay State Department official |url=https://www.washingtonblade.com/2025/10/20/vance-swears-in-gay-state-department-official/ |date=October 20, 2025}}</ref><ref name="techtransparency" /> [[Mike Kelly (Australian politician)|Mike Kelly]] is president of Palantir Australia.<ref>{{cite web |website=Palantir Blog |title=Kelly Explains His Decision to Join Palantir |url=https://www.palantir.com/kelly-explains-his-decision-to-join-palantir/ |access-date=October 22, 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Palantir Technologies Australia |url=https://www.defenceconnect.com.au/joint-capabilites/8695-a-data-driven-information-architecture-for-defence |work=Defence Connect |date=September 1, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230802171755/https://www.defenceconnect.com.au/joint-capabilites/8695-a-data-driven-information-architecture-for-defence |archive-date=August 2, 2023 |language=en-gb}}</ref> He served as Parliamentary Secretary for Defence from 2011 to 2013 and [[Minister for Defence Industry|Minister for Defence Materiel]] in 2013.<ref>{{cite web |title=Parliamentary Handbook |url=https://handbook.aph.gov.au/parliamentarians/HRI |website=handbook.aph.gov.au |access-date=October 22, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251022032753/https://web.archive.org/screenshot/https://handbook.aph.gov.au/parliamentarians/HRI |archive-date=October 22, 2025}}</ref> [[Matthew Turpin]], former director for China at the [[United States National Security Council|White House National Security Council]] and senior advisor for China to the [[United States Secretary of Commerce|Secretary of Commerce]] during the [[First presidency of Donald Trump|first Trump administration]], serves as senior advisor.<ref name=":02">{{Cite web |title=Matthew Turpin |url=https://www.hoover.org/profiles/matthew-turpin |access-date=November 18, 2023 |publisher=Hoover Institution |language=en |archive-date=November 18, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231118223309/https://www.hoover.org/profiles/matthew-turpin |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=July 14, 2021 |title=China expert Matt Turpin on Beijing's strategic objectives – "Intelligence Matters" – CBS News |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/china-strategic-objectives-intelligence-matters/ |access-date=November 18, 2023 |publisher=CBS News |archive-date=November 18, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231118223305/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/china-strategic-objectives-intelligence-matters/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

