===Voting structure===
Palantir has a special voting structure, tied to the classification of shares into Class A, Class B and Class F. The Class F shares, totaling 1,005,000, are managed by the Founder Voting Trust and owned equally by the three founders Thiel, Karp, and Cohen, which ensures them a 49.99% voting interest regardless of the number of other shares they hold or the number of new shares the company issues.<ref name="BloombergSankar">{{cite news |last1=Sloan |first1=Dylan |last2=Carson |first2=Biz |title=Palantir's 525% Stock Surge Makes CTO Shyam Sankar the Firm's Fifth Billionaire |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-08-04/palantir-s-chief-tech-officer-becomes-a-billionaire-as-stock-hits-new-high |date=August 4, 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250804132233/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-08-04/palantir-s-chief-tech-officer-becomes-a-billionaire-as-stock-hits-new-high |archive-date=August 4, 2025}}</ref><ref name="barrons">{{cite news |last1=Lin |first1=Ed |title=Palantir Chairman Peter Thiel to Sell Up to $1 Billion of Stock |url=https://www.barrons.com/amp/articles/palantir-stock-sell-peter-thiel-fb7bc3aa |website=Barron's |date=September 10, 2024 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20240911160704/https://www.barrons.com/articles/palantir-stock-sell-peter-thiel-fb7bc3aa |archive-date=September 11, 2024 |language=en-us}}</ref><ref name="businessinsidermulticlass">{{cite news |last1=Wolverton |first1=Troy |title=Palantir will have a stock structure that ensures its 3 founders will remain in control 'for the foreseeable future' |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/palantir-multi-class-stock-structure-leaves-founders-in-control-2020-8 |work=Business Insider |date=August 26, 2020 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20241001052355/https://www.businessinsider.com/palantir-multi-class-stock-structure-leaves-founders-in-control-2020-8 |archive-date=October 1, 2024}}</ref> In response to criticism that the founders wanted to remain "emperors for life", they said the creation of the Class F shares did not violate the law or the company charter and had been approved by a majority of other Palantir investors when the firm went public in 2020.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Leonard |first1=Mike |title=Peter Thiel, Palantir Co-Founders Slam 'Emperor for Life' Claims |url=https://news.bloomberglaw.com/esg/peter-thiel-palantir-co-founders-slam-emperor-for-life-claims |date=July 24, 2021 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20241024182341/https://news.bloomberglaw.com/esg/peter-thiel-palantir-co-founders-slam-emperor-for-life-claims |archive-date=October 24, 2024}}</ref> In 2025, ''[[Bloomberg News|Bloomberg]]'' wrote:
{{blockquote|Because of the company's growing role in world affairs, super voting shares also confer real power onto Thiel, Karp and Cohen that will extend to the company's relationships with militaries and other agencies.}} 
{{blockquote|That could come in handy if, say, the company received a takeover bid from a foreign adversary. And it could prevent the company from bending to pressure from bad actors, domestically or otherwise, while allowing management to stay the course on long-term plans. But it also insulates an increasingly powerful company from a measure of accountability offered by the public markets.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Chapman |first1=Lizette |title=Palantir Stock Structure Gives Founders the Power to Stay the Course |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2025-07-30/palantir-stock-structure-gives-founders-the-power-to-stay-the-course |date=30 July 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250730233624/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2025-07-30/palantir-stock-structure-gives-founders-the-power-to-stay-the-course#selection-1777.147-1781.381 |archive-date=30 July 2025}}</ref>}}

The founders, executives, and "insiders" also hold Class B shares, each of which carries ten votes, while the publicly traded Class A shares carry only one vote each. Class B shares can be converted to Class A shares on a 1-to-1 basis to be sold to outsiders.<ref name="barrons"/><ref name="BloombergSankar"/><ref name="businessinsidermulticlass"/><ref>{{cite news |last1=Lin |first1=Ed |title=Palantir CEO Alex Karp Ends Plan to Sell Stock |url=https://www.barrons.com/articles/palantir-stock-ceo-alex-karp-9d18d2c0 |work=Barron's |date=May 6, 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250506145642/https://www.barrons.com/articles/palantir-stock-ceo-alex-karp-9d18d2c0 |archive-date=May 6, 2025 |language=en-us}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=SEC FORM 4 |url=https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1321655/000132165525000113/xslF345X05/wk-form4_1755906867.xml |publisher=Securities and Exchange Commission |access-date=October 28, 2025}}</ref>

